cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "VarVAMP Assay Design and In Silico Validation Workflow"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Faham"
    given-names: "Aymane"

version: 1.2.0

date-released: 2026-09-02

license: GPL-3.0-or-later

repository-code: "https://github.com/Epigenome-Sb/varVAMP-qPCR-workflow"

url: "https://github.com/Epigenome-Sb/varVAMP-qPCR-workflow"

abstract: >-
  An interactive and reproducible command-line workflow for nucleotide
  sequence preprocessing, multiple sequence alignment, conservation analysis,
  assay design with VarVAMP, and in silico validation of PCR and qPCR assays.
  The workflow supports VarVAMP SINGLE, QPCR, and TILED modes and integrates
  MAFFT, MARS, SeqKit, CD-HIT-EST, trimAl, VarVAMP, MFEprimer, and BLAST+.
  It provides explicit scientific parameter checkpoints, reproducible
  workflow metadata, primer-pair target-coverage analysis, and detailed
  evaluation of qPCR probes, including expansion and comparison of
  IUPAC-degenerate probe variants.

keywords:
  - PCR
  - qPCR
  - primer design
  - probe design
  - in silico validation
